ve a material impact on our consolidated financial statements.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":307,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038444","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001473334","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1473334/000149315226038444/form10-q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1f3dd8362b88082a05a7369c8b5a22dae6b89162c769fa805121b5eac770b361.bin","sha256":"1f3dd8362b88082a05a7369c8b5a22dae6b89162c769fa805121b5eac770b361"}},{"id":"035573d6805cc3311bc6d3df7aa1b03d827bc4e481b1692d61038519f9f35d39","quote":"The Company’s management does not believe that any other recently issued, but not yet effective, authoritative guidance, if currently adopted, would have a material impact on the Company’s financial statement presentation or disclosures.","context":"In April 2026, the FASB issued ASU 2026-01—Equity (Topic 505): Initial Measurement of Paid-in-Kind Dividends on Equity-Classified Preferred Stock. The amendments in this Update clarify the initial measurement of paid-in-kind dividends on preferred stock that is classified within equity. The amendments in this Update are effective for all entities for annual reporting periods beginning after December 15, 2026, and interim reporting periods within those annual reporting periods. Early adoption is permitted in any interim or annual reporting period in which financial statements have not yet been issued or made available for issuance. An entity adopting the amendments in an interim reporting period should apply them as of the beginning of the annual reporting period that includes that interim reporting period. The Company is currently evaluating the impact that the adoption of ASU 2026-01 will have on its consolidated financial statement presentation or disclosures.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":308,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038444","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001473334","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1473334/000149315226038444/form10-q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1f3dd8362b88082a05a7369c8b5a22dae6b89162c769fa805121b5eac770b361.bin","sha256":"1f3dd8362b88082a05a7369c8b5a22dae6b89162c769fa805121b5eac770b361"}},{"id":"e1b2524e0cdfea853d8b9073aa9136fa23550d0404532d06952cf6713ab5e11b","quote":"Note 3 - Inventories","context":"The Company’s management does not believe that any other recently issued, but not yet effective, authoritative guidance, if currently adopted, would have a material impact on the Company’s financial statement presentation or disclosures.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":309,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038444","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001473334","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1473334/000149315226038444/form10-q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1f3dd8362b88082a05a7369c8b5a22dae6b89162c769fa805121b5eac770b361.bin","sha256":"1f3dd8362b88082a05a7369c8b5a22dae6b89162c769fa805121b5eac770b361"}},{"id":"0e99fbff6a9321d82564986b3b84dc3f5c1c3caaec299af0d27864952c53e29d","quote":"The inventories as of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025 totaled $1,935,880 and $2,163,437, respectively, and consisted entirely of finished goods.","context":"Note 3 - Inventories","section":"Segment Reporting","block":310,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038444","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001473334","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1473334/000149315226038444/form10-q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/1f3dd8362b88082a05a7369c8b5